@inherits LocalizedComponent

@*
    The playground's counterpart to the site's sitewide footer (apps/site/src/components/
    Footer.astro) — same links, same copy, kept in sync by hand because Astro and Blazor
    share no rendering system to render one component from (see the KNOWN DUPLICATION note
    on `site.legal.entity` in `site.ts`).

    A component of its own, not markup inlined into MainLayout, for the same reason
    SiteHeader and BrandHeading already are: it has to redraw when LocaleState.Changed
    fires, and MainLayout is a LayoutComponentBase — it cannot also inherit
    LocalizedComponent to pick up that subscription itself.

    Root-relative links only (`/about/`, `/fr/about/`, …), never relative:
    `wwwroot/index.html` sets `<base href="/playground/" />`, so a relative "about" would
    resolve to `/playground/about` — a page that does not exist — while a leading-slash
    path ignores that base and correctly reaches the Astro site, served from the same
    artefact, at the same root (§12.2). `Pages/NotFound.razor`'s own "go back to the
    site" link already relies on the same rule.

    Rendered from MainLayout only, not BareLayout: BareLayout renders `/hero`, the widget
    embedded in the landing page's own hero, which is chromeless by design — it already
    sits inside a page that carries the real footer around it, so a second one here would
    be a duplicate, not a consistency.

    The copyright year reads `DateTime.Now.Year`, not a build timestamp, and that is a real
    divergence from Footer.astro rather than a rounding of one. Footer.astro reads its own
    build's timestamp instead of `Date.now()` so that a same-source rebuild cannot show a
    different year than the one before it — a reproducibility discipline, not an attempt to
    be right about today's date. This is a WebAssembly app with no build-time value of its
    own to freeze, and the only candidate, the site's `/version.json`, would turn a footer
    that renders synchronously into one that waits on a fetch.

    So from the first of January until the next deploy the two footers name different years,
    and that window is not one evening: this site ships on `release/*` tags rather than on a
    clock, so it lasts as long as the gap between releases. The site names the year it was
    built in; the playground names the year the reader is actually in. The playground's is
    the one that is right, which is why the fetch is not worth paying for — reading
    `/version.json` would not make the year correct, it would only spread the site's frozen
    one to a second place. `tests/browser/chrome-parity.spec.ts` compares these two footers
    and normalises the digits out of the copyright line for exactly this reason.
*@

<footer class="site-footer">
    <nav class="footer-nav" aria-label='@PlaygroundStrings.T(LocaleState.Current, "footer.nav")'>
        <a href="@ApiHref">@PlaygroundStrings.T(LocaleState.Current, "footer.api")</a>
        <a href="@ReleaseNotesHref">@PlaygroundStrings.T(LocaleState.Current, "footer.releaseNotes")</a>
        <span class="divider" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <a href="@AboutHref">@PlaygroundStrings.T(LocaleState.Current, "footer.about")</a>
        <a href="@PrivacyHref">@PlaygroundStrings.T(LocaleState.Current, "footer.privacy")</a>
    </nav>
    <p class="copyright">© @DateTime.Now.Year @Entity</p>
</footer>

@code {

    // Mirrored from `site.legal.entity` in `site.ts` — the KNOWN DUPLICATION documented
    // there, restated as a named constant rather than a bare literal so the mirroring is
    // visible here too, not only in the comment on the other side of it.
    private const string Entity = "REEFACT";

    private string AboutHref => LocaleState.Current == Locale.Fr ? "/fr/about/" : "/about/";
    private string ApiHref => LocaleState.Current == Locale.Fr ? "/fr/api/" : "/api/";
    private string ReleaseNotesHref => LocaleState.Current == Locale.Fr ? "/fr/release-notes/" : "/release-notes/";
    private string PrivacyHref => LocaleState.Current == Locale.Fr ? "/fr/privacy/" : "/privacy/";

}
